<title>CHILE: Genesis Chile Fund denies sales speculation.</title>
<headline>Genesis Chile Fund denies sales speculation.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Speculation that rattled the bolsa in the last two sessions that the Genesis Chile Fund is selling a large part of its portfolio is false, said the fund's Chilean representative Christopher Brown.</p>
<p>&quot;There is no truth in the rumor the we are reducing the fund and much less that we are taking it back to England,&quot; Brown told Reuters.</p>
<p>Traders said fears that the $450 million fund was reducing its stock portfolio have hurt Chile blue chips, which have lost 1.5 percent in since Thursday's close.  </p>
<p>Brown said sales and purchases by the London-quoted fund are part of normal portfolio adjustment.</p>
<p>-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212</p>
</text>
